    },
    {
      "id": "5gd0al2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Magnetism"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1ybak1c",
      "content": "Magnetism is the property of materials that attract iron and other magnetic materials."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "moy2v1j",
      "content": "Magnets have two poles: North pole and South pole."
    },
    {
      "id": "c7ipnju",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Properties of Magnets"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2udgmcj",
      "content": "• Like poles repel each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5lxc3uw",
      "content": "• Unlike poles attract each other."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j6fab04",
      "content": "• Magnetic poles always exist in pairs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jnk0a6d",
      "content": "• Magnetic force is strongest at the poles."
    },
    {
      "id": "ryayhxb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Electromagnet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kxbkbk9",
      "content": "An electromagnet is a magnet produced by passing electric current through a coil of wire."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2q7lepw",
      "content": "Applications:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "SI Units of electrical quantities (Current: Ampere, Resistance: Ohm, Potential Difference: Volt, Power: Watt) are frequently asked in RRB and SSC exams.",
        "Numerical questions involving Ohm's Law (V = IR) and equivalent resistance calculations in Series and Parallel circuits.",
        "Properties of magnetic field lines and the distinction between permanent magnets and electromagnets are popular conceptual questions."
      ],
      "id": "ib0tuhr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hpjkiee",
      "content": "• Electric bell"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bbcl30g",
      "content": "• Electric motors"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2jilmec",
      "content": "• Magnetic cranes"
    },
    {
      "id": "4as4iqy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "azv33hq",
      "content": "• SI unit of electric current is Ampere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ow8v1m1",
      "content": "• Ohm’s law formula is V = IR."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0zaqsi9",
      "content": "• SI unit of resistance is Ohm."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9fuorh4",
      "content": "• Like poles repel and unlike poles attract."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}